 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? The traditional 50-50 split is only one way to go about it. Are there any reasons why one parent should lead on living expenses rather than the big day? Then ask them if they have a preference. It matters a lot. Not rude at all. Just polite and curious. Do they want to cover their share of the wedding you' set up for yourself? That's the polite thing to do. Then ask them to imagine if the tables were turned. Would they expect you to pick up the whole wedding because they couldn't afford their share?",
